27833      title 'Gasoline and Emissions Data';
27834      data gas;
27835      set sashelp.gas;
27836      if fuel in ('Ethanol', '82rongas', 'Gasohol');
27837      run;

NOTE: There were 171 observations read from the data set SASHELP.GAS.
NOTE: The data set WORK.GAS has 112 observations and 4 variables.

27838      ods graphics on;
27839      * Request a Spline Transformation of Equivalence Ratio;
27840      proc transreg data=Gas solve ss2 plots=(transformation obp residuals);
27841      model identity(nox) = spline(EqRatio / nknots=4);
27842      run;

NOTE: 2 observations were deleted from the analysis due to missing values.
NOTE: Algorithm converged.
NOTE: There were 112 observations read from the data set WORK.GAS.
NOTE: The PROCEDURE TRANSREG printed page 1714.

27843      * Separate Curves and Intercepts;
27844      proc transreg data=Gas solve ss2 additive plots=(transformation obp);
27845      model identity(nox) = class(Fuel / zero=none) |
27846      spline(EqRatio / nknots=4 after);
27847      run;

NOTE: Since the model contains SMOOTH, BSPLINE, PBSPLINE, or a CLASS expansion with ZERO=NONE, a model with an implicit intercept is fit.
NOTE: All statistics are mean corrected.
NOTE: 2 observations were deleted from the analysis due to missing values.
NOTE: Algorithm converged.
NOTE: There were 112 observations read from the data set WORK.GAS.
NOTE: The PROCEDURE TRANSREG printed page 1715.

27848      * Separate Intercepts;
27849      proc transreg data=Gas solve ss2 additive;
27850      model identity(nox) = class(Fuel / zero=none)
27851      spline(EqRatio / nknots=4);
27852      run;

NOTE: Since the model contains SMOOTH, BSPLINE, PBSPLINE, or a CLASS expansion with ZERO=NONE, a model with an implicit intercept is fit.
NOTE: All statistics are mean corrected.
NOTE: 2 observations were deleted from the analysis due to missing values.
NOTE: Algorithm converged.
NOTE: There were 112 observations read from the data set WORK.GAS.
NOTE: The PROCEDURE TRANSREG printed page 1716.

27853      * Separate Curves and Intercepts with Penalized B-Splines;
27854      proc transreg data=Gas ss2 plots=transformation lprefix=0;
27855      model identity(nox) = class(Fuel / zero=none) * pbspline(EqRatio);
27856      run;

NOTE: AFTER is assumed when PBSPLINE is crossed with a CLASS variable.
NOTE: Since the model contains SMOOTH, BSPLINE, PBSPLINE, or a CLASS expansion with ZERO=NONE, a model with an implicit intercept is fit.
NOTE: All statistics are mean corrected.
NOTE: 2 observations were deleted from the analysis due to missing values.
NOTE: Algorithm converged.
NOTE: There were 112 observations read from the data set WORK.GAS.
NOTE: The PROCEDURE TRANSREG printed page 1717.

27857      title 'Introductory Main-Effects ANOVA Example';
27858      data a;
27859      input y x1 $ x2 $;
27860      datalines;

NOTE: The data set WORK.A has 12 observations and 3 variables.

27873      ;
27874      * Fit a main-effects ANOVA model with 1, 0, -1 coding;
27875      proc transreg ss2;
27876      model identity(y) = class(x1 x2 / effects);
27877      output coefficients replace;
27878      run;

NOTE: The data set WORK.DATA37 has 14 observations and 9 variables.
